From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scratch <a@b.c>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:47:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] Android: resolution list offers fractions of the native
 size and resizes the surface in place

SDL lists only the native display mode on Android. The settings window offers 100% down to 25% of it, applied at once, through
SDLActivity.setSurfaceResolution; the stored mouse position is scaled with the new window size.
As on the desktop, a smaller resolution makes the interface larger on the screen. The settings window's gamma slider,
which does nothing on Android, sets the interface scale ([GUI] scaling factor) instead, laid out again at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
